== Basic Text Escapes

This has a \* literal asterisk, not bold.

This has a \_ literal underscore, not italic.

This has a \` literal backtick, not code.

This has a \# literal hash, not an expression.

This is a \\ literal backslash.

== Mixed Formatting

This is *bold with \* escaped asterisk inside*.

This is _italic with \_ escaped underscore inside_.

This is `code with \` escaped backtick`.

== String Literal Escapes

#let msg = "Hello \"world\" with escaped quotes"

#let path = "C:\\Users\\Documents\\file.txt"

#let multiline = "Line 1\nLine 2\nLine 3"

#let tab = "Column1\tColumn2\tColumn3"

== Complex Cases

This text has \*\*double escaped asterisks\*\*.

Mixing: *bold text with \* escaped* and normal \* escaped.

Edge case: backslash at end\\

#let complex = "String with \"quotes\", \\backslashes\\, and \nnewlines"

== All Escapes Together

Text: \* \_ \` \# \\

String: #let all = "\* \_ \` \# \\ \" \n \t \r"

== Should Still Work

*Actually bold*

_Actually italic_

`Actually code`

#let x = 42

Regular text with #x interpolation.
